6;zUhci9Hwt137LMl7qZkge2CELC2ufK3Em7_1iNxWPrIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx2026-07-20T23:57:20.601Zƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bnPqZInmkynazUhD9pQbXBplvwnjzaVzWBFZTU6tPZwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxxhttps://www.culturalsurvival.org/news/bridging-tradition-and-technology-1st-meeting-indigenous-youth-communicators-bahiaƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;YVK24zyrLwrpDHXcvYqqwXyWtfKGx-STz4wNKIsQxEwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9https://newscable-source-broker.invalid/activitypub/actorƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bqltPbx0eOwVcWljXKqUs4q07zOa-lxtxB8y6nGE8Dcƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ZrG2g9VhvCs6rA9YZhc9bteJ-UQNYKmPWp2eAlqZSlAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxxhttps://www.culturalsurvival.org/news/bridging-tradition-and-technology-1st-meeting-indigenous-youth-communicators-bahiaƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;PNjXOM_NrthTU_eNySN5w7UV6BuZYC7SCc_z5lbpVSIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyG<span>Bridging Tradition and Technology: The 1st Meeting of Indigenous Youth Communicators of Bahia</span> <div class="field field--name-taxonomy-vocabulary-8 field--type-entity-reference field--label-above"> <div class="field__label">Country</div> <div class="field__items "> <div class="field__item"><a href="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/country/brazil" hreflang="en">Brazil</a></div> </div> </div> <span><span>agnes</span></span> <span><time datetime="2026-07-17T18:43:51-04:00" title="Friday, July 17, 2026 - 18:43">Fri, 07/17/2026 - 18:43</time> </span> <div class="field field--name-taxonomy-vocabulary-14 field--type-entity-reference field--label-above"> <div class="field__label">Issues</div> <div class="field__items "> <div class="field__item"><a href="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/issues/human-rights" hreflang="en">Human Rights</a></div> </div> </div> <div class="field field--name-field-program field--type-list-string field--label-inline clearfix"> <div class="field__label d-inline-block">Program</div> <div class="field__items d-inline-block"> <div class="field__item">5</div> </div> </div> <div class="field field--name-field-image-item field--type-image field--label-above"> <div class="field__label">Main Image</div> <div class="field__items "> <div class="field__item"> <img loading="eager" srcset="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/styles/max_325x325/public/2%20%284%29.jpg?itok=JEatWZ0L 325w, https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/styles/max_650x650/public/2%20%284%29.jpg?itok=8lSSC1ix 650w, https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/styles/max_1300x1300/public/2%20%284%29.jpg?itok=dkDh5RIc 1300w, https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/styles/max_1920x1920/public/2%20%284%29.jpg?itok=Z-J44YV5 1920w, https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/styles/max_2600x2600/public/2%20%284%29.jpg?itok=BOS55zJu 2600w" sizes="(min-width: 1290px) 1290px, 100vw" src="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/styles/max_325x325/public/2%20%284%29.jpg?itok=JEatWZ0L" alt class="img-responsive"> </div> </div> </div> <div class="field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"><p dir="ltr"><strong>By Angel Ferreira </strong>(PayayÃ¡, CS Intern)</p> <p>On July 10-12, 2026, the PayayÃ¡ Territory, located in the municipality of Utinga, the gateway to Chapada Diamantina in Brazil, became the epicenter of ancestral communication and resistance for Indigenous Peoples. The 1st Meeting of Indigenous Youth Communicators of Bahia brought together leaders, Elders, youth from various ethnic groups, and partner organizations with a clear objective: to strengthen the defense of their territories through communication.</p> <p>Organized by the Indigenous Youth Council of Bahia (COJIBA), the event combined the power of new media with the wisdom of the Elders, consolidating communication as a vital tool for struggle and cultural preservation.</p> <p><img alt="img" data-entity-type="file" data-entity-uuid="f1fe7698-a138-4c81-a53d-5398903b8472" src="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/inline-images/7%20%281%29.jpg" width="1280" height="1920" loading="lazy"></p> <p>The gathering began with traditional arrival rituals, connecting participants to the spirituality and soil of the PayayÃ¡ land. The hospitality of the host community was also reflected in the local cuisine. Participants were welcomed with rich, traditional meals from the region, including <em>banana moqueca</em> (a traditional plantain stew) and cuscuz with<em> licuri</em> (steamed cornmeal with licuri palm nut), along with local fruits.</p> <p>More than just moments of leisure, the guided walks through the territory functioned as practical lessons in historical and environmental contextualization. Each natural space visited carried a profound explanation of its ecological and sacred importance to the PayayÃ¡ people.<br> &nbsp;</p> <p><img alt="img" data-entity-type="file" data-entity-uuid="b6411558-de2b-4e48-b881-b172282176a1" src="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/inline-images/1%20%283%29.jpg" width="1920" height="1280" loading="lazy"></p> <p>Chief Juvenal PayayÃ¡ was a prominent presence at the event, sharing ancestral stories and reinforcing the importance of recording and spreading these memories through the hands of the Indigenous people themselves.&nbsp;"The Meeting of Youth Communicators here in the PayayÃ¡ Territory, I believe, is a significant milestone for the entire Indigenous movement," shared Chief Juvenal PayayÃ¡.</p> <p>During the three days of immersion, the program featured dialogue circles on cosmovisions and practical workshops focused on digital content production, photography, and journalistic coverage techniques.</p> <p><img alt="ing" data-entity-type="file" data-entity-uuid="f26e81b2-eb41-4818-86d7-039f47c41849" src="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/inline-images/10%20%283%29.jpg" width="1280" height="1920" loading="lazy"></p> <p>However, the debate went beyond technical skills. One of the central points of the panel discussions addressed the political role and responsibility of being an Indigenous communicator. In a scenario of growing territorial disputes, the safety of these young people was also a top priority. Participants discussed strategies for digital and physical protection against threats and retaliation faced by those who denounce human rights violations in their communities.</p> <p>By unifying technology and tradition, COJIBA and the young participants took a crucial step toward ensuring that narratives about the Indigenous Peoples of Bahia are increasingly told in the first person. The 1st Meeting of Indigenous Youth Communicators of Bahia concluded not only with more qualified communicators, but also with a strengthened network of support and mutual protection, ready to echo the voices and resistance of Bahian villages to the world.</p> <p><img alt="img" data-entity-type="file" data-entity-uuid="d6f61309-cf78-41c4-8eef-5c280064b9dd" src="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/inline-images/6%20%282%29.jpg" width="1280" height="1920" loading="lazy"></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><img alt="img" data-entity-type="file" data-entity-uuid="bcc9821e-075d-43c8-a149-f4b5afb3edba" src="https://www.culturalsurvival.org/sites/default/files/inline-images/4%20%284%29.jpg" width="1280" height="1920" loading="lazy"></p> </div>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;g0-tyXuXoNOU8zfkcWYXSk8VBRwIy_XFtsCvGo_dUPYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;XpUILMrNoR7jGROhULR0UBKcQayLELl21MCBkTgQotoƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-SZkq5Qq15Au0DGDL7gF5XG12bQIcY6S_rZcH8-wU7kƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;yosZ5N6CqBbWxdyLPIrMT8wiJNCGE5I6pouhpgWd5HAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Al0eK97Q1Am8oQI70s2R6d8gNgHFp87SClzyk4Zidygƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;7IX_ZWiUN7VoAwJn2qPjt32CjCeJw_SlS4G0pB5PDjYƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bBL9W8fO7WrGyx9WOgofz1BfKB1hrKbOjNyWxHet9Rwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;VdxwTOlkHFyS5hlnlk9J-JExwEo0NN3SgyTRaF7BW3Uƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqSyndicationSourceƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2y_aPjBbxGKSfT7aKaNriCcrTeFfGw9buEp18TG5Lm0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx(urn:rmn:predicate:source-reports-summaryƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4OpLFS741U-ugkjDprmc4ZSZTO2iN5XtzraP_9uYakcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarktUnsaturatedPredicateƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DbeFYn6UHU93ozunBSW4btibeb_gBpx-C098WukkOf4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarduni